Subject: [PATCH] Admit stopping an inactive Layer transition during KAG restore
Tested-by: M5 full KAG slot/visual/audio/call-stack restore instrumentation
Tested-by: tests/test_krkr_tjs2_source_admission.py focused git-apply unittest and forced Android CMake configure

KAG restoreFlags stops all transitions before restoring any layer. Android's
selected display backend cannot start transitions, so stopping an inactive
transition succeeds after validating the native Layer. Active transition
creation remains an explicit unsupported operation until M6.

diff --git a/src/core/visual/LayerIntf.cpp b/src/core/visual/LayerIntf.cpp
--- a/src/core/visual/LayerIntf.cpp
+++ b/src/core/visual/LayerIntf.cpp
@@ -9302,7 +9302,8 @@
 TJS_BEGIN_NATIVE_METHOD_DECL(stopTransition)
 {
-	TJS_eTJSError(TJS_W("Unsupported M2 method: stopTransition"));
-	return TJS_E_NOTIMPL;
+	TJS_GET_NATIVE_INSTANCE(_this, tTJSNI_Layer);
+	_this->StopTransition();
+	return TJS_S_OK;
 }
 TJS_END_NATIVE_METHOD_DECL(stopTransition)
 #endif
